The README's own opening states the rule it is violating: *"Architectural debt MUST NOT exist only
inside conversation history — PAEOS-0 axiom A2 ... undocumented compromises are exactly the failure
PAEOS exists to prevent."* Twenty-five compromises are recorded as index lines pointing at nothing.

`operations/ENGINEERING_LIFECYCLE.md:189` defines the L15 failure mode as *"stale/missing ledger
update → incident (undocumented change)."* This is that incident, standing open, at scale.

Corroborating: `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_ATLAS.md` declares itself *"Governed by state L15 — updated
