## §4. Candidates

Three candidates, each a **single missing canonical layer**, ordered by chain position. No
cross-cutting capability is proposed; per stage instruction the field is restricted to the fixed
19-layer set.

---

### Candidate A — **L07 Trade-off Mitigation (`StageId.MITIGATION`)**

**DAG position (Q3).** Chain slot 8 of 21, between `TRADEOFF` (built) and `DESIGN` (built). It is
**the first fully-missing layer** and the only missing layer whose *both* neighbours already exist
— so it is the only candidate that can be inserted with zero new upstream or downstream work.

**Upstream dependencies (Q6).** None missing. L06 `TRADEOFF` supplies the required entry artifact
(the matrix). L08 `DESIGN` is the ready consumer. Self-contained.

**What it must produce.** Per `operations/ENGINEERING_LIFECYCLE.md:105-112`: a **mitigation
catalogue** — kill switches, fallback behaviour, shadow mode, safety constraints. Exit guard: every
high-severity trade-off carries a named safeguard *or* an accepted-risk record. Irreversible
accepted-risks escalate to a founder Decision.

**If deferred (Q4).** F4 persists: `DESIGN` continues to run with an unmet constitutional entry
condition indefinitely, and `TRADEOFF → DESIGN` remains an illegal edge. Every risk the L06 matrix
surfaces is discarded at the moment it is identified — the system enumerates its own hazards and
then throws them away. Worse, deferral is self-concealing: because `runtime/mitigation.py` exists
(F3), each subsequent audit is likelier to mark L07 done and move on.

**What gets easier if built first (Q5).** L08 gains its constitutional input, sharpening every
downstream design. L09 `CRITIQUE` and L10/L14 adversarial review gain a concrete falsification
target ("is this safeguard real?") far more tractable than critiquing prose. Most importantly it
establishes the *pattern* for the remaining three layers: `RoleSpec` + orchestrator slot +
artifact obligation + gate. L15/L18/L19 all become instances of a proven template.

**Clean implementability (Q7).** **Highest of the three.** Requires: a `_MITIGATION` `RoleSpec`
(role `PLANNER`, per lifecycle *"Planner + Adversary"*; write scope `mitigation/`; read scope
including `tradeoff` outputs), one `ROLE_SPECS` entry, one line in the `_run_body` stage tuple
between `TRADEOFF` and `DESIGN`, and replacement of the `runtime/mitigation.py` vacuum. Context
already chains forward via `planner_artifacts` (`:254`, `:271`) so the matrix reaches it and the
catalogue reaches `DESIGN` for free.

**Shortcut risk.** One, and it is real: the exit guard *"every high-severity risk mitigated or
accepted-risk recorded"* is a semantic predicate. Implemented as a prose artifact with no
obligation, L07 becomes ceremony — a stage that always passes. The design must bind a
`required_evidence` obligation (`_RE_DERIVE`/`_IDEATE` at `agents/__init__.py:65` and `:92` are the
in-repo precedent; note `_RESEARCH`, `_CRITIQUE` and `_TRADEOFF` were all shipped with
`required_evidence=()` — the drift is already underway and L07 should not extend it).

**Self-hosting contribution (Q1/Q2).** Indirect but structural. L07 does not itself close the
self-hosting loop; it removes the first illegal edge, which is a precondition for ever routing the
autonomous walk through `Gate.propose_transition` (F2). While *any* illegal edge remains, enabling
the gate on the autonomous path halts the loop. **L07 is therefore the first prerequisite for
kernel-enforced self-construction.**

